--- !u!1001 &1832558764
PrefabInstance:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  serializedVersion: 2
  m_Modification:
    serializedVersion: 3
    m_TransformParent: {fileID: 0}
    m_Modifications:
    - target: {fileID: 4613828026226185999, guid: 3b2842f6aeffbd24cac0d9e63051d100, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_Text
      value: "Hand in hand with the somber horizon lies the deep sea, so blue and
        grand. \nThese eyes of his won't capture the view, from where he lay still
        in the sand. \n\nEven so, the waves continue to flow. In the past he had
        awoken from a strange glow, thinking he was alone. \nAt the door however
        there stood a man with a broken bone.\n\nTo this stranger he offered his
        aid, \nunknowing that a price would be paid. \nThrough weather clear and
        clouded the stranger spoke of tales from the lands of opportunity, the man
        slowly yearning for a sense of unity. \n\nOn that fair summer day the sounds
        of the tweeting dove and rustling of waves against the sand slowly faded,
        as he left behind his home by the sea. \nAt first the towering concrete beasts
        threatened that which he was familiar with, \nthe place he once found himself
        was just a myth.\n\nSenses deafened, mind clouded by new sound, \nonly with
        eyes he searched and found. \nThe one known as a friend, gave him company,
        \nsomething he had never known or understood. \nThe day he was brought to
        the company before a door of darkness he stood. \n\nDay after day, working,
        struggling, hurting, the one called his friend holding him like a chain.
        Through all the pain, \nhe found no reason to stay. \n\nThe only way out,
        \npushing another down the final route. \nCalled once his friend the man
        now gone, \nby the hand of the one now forced to press on. \nHunted with
        nowhere to go, the man now stood in line to the fields of death."
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 7544921937658798171, guid: 3b2842f6aeffbd24cac0d9e63051d100, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_Name
      value: Note (1)
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
